                    "value": "Why two CAC proxies? Marketing ÷ net adds treats every new subscriber as growth, which implies zero churn and contradicts the churn used in LTV. The realistic proxy adds back the subscribers the assumed churn rate says must be replaced, so LTV and CAC rest on the same assumption. Sales & marketing data starts in 2023. Churn is a hypothetical assumption and CAC figures are proxies (all sales & marketing spend / subscribers added). Spotify does not disclose either.",
